sentences.text:
5. Being aggrieved of the aforesaid order, the petitioners have assailed the same on primarily following grounds:-
(i) That the impugned order is not based on sound principles of law and is arbitrary,
illegal, unjust and perverse;
(ii) That Ld. Trial Court grossly erred in not considering the fact that there was no evidence against petitioner no. 2 and she was earlier kept in column no. 12 by the IO;
Nasreen Akhtar vs State on 14 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32191487/
3 (iii) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that the allegations and avernments made in the complaint are contradictory and not trust worthy;
(iv) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that there was no MLC or medical record in support of the allegations levelled by the complainant;
(v) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that both the petitioners are residents of Hyderabad, Telangana and it is extremely difficult for them to face trial in this case at Delhi;

